; A clock line's time is followed by one separator byte and then the
; account.  When that byte is a TAB rather than a space, the account,
; payee and note still read as they do after a space.  The journal is
; test/regress/timelog-tab-separator.dat (see its header for why).

test -f test/regress/timelog-tab-separator.dat reg --format "%(date)|%(payee)|%(account)|%(note)|%(amount)\n"
2024/01/18|Tab payee|Epsilon|tabbed|3600s
end test

test -f test/regress/timelog-tab-separator.dat bal
               1.00h  Epsilon
end test
